{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetry"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.energySlope_convex_le_two_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.energySlope_convex_le_two_log","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryLogBound.lean#L85-L106","doc":"**Invariant (1), pinned: `δ ≤ 2 ln q` for every convex interface weight.**\nAt `q₀` the bound is `0.2087`, attained at `w = 0`; the corpus sits at\n`-0.0218`. Through `bondSum_wellMixed_symmetry` the symmetry coefficient of\n*any* convex interface on a degree-`k` well-mixed graph is at most\n`(k/2)·ln q` per unit `E₀` — one order of magnitude below the SEMF target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.half_splitting_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.half_splitting_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryLogBound.lean#L70-L83","doc":"With the pinned bonds `b_pp = q²/[2]_q`, `b_nn = q⁻²/[2]_q`, half the\nlike-species splitting is exactly `2 ln q`: `b_pp/b_nn = q⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.energySlope_convex_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.energySlope_convex_le","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryLogBound.lean#L56-L68","doc":"**Invariant (1): the convex family bounds the slope.** For every weight in\n`[0, 1]`, `δ ≤ (e_nn - e_pp)/2`, with equality at `w = 0` (pure `σ⁻¹`\ninterface). The *sign* can be flipped by a weight below the crossing; the\n*magnitude* cannot exceed half the like-species splitting, whatever the weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.interface_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.interface_mem","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryLogBound.lean#L50-L54","doc":"For a convex weight the interface lies between the two like-species bonds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.energySlope_eq_log_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.energySlope_eq_log_form","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryLogBound.lean#L42-L48","doc":"`energySlope` in `e = -ln b` letters is `SymmetrySignAmGm.delta` — the same\nnumber, so the AM-vs-GM sign result transfers verbatim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.interface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound.interface","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryLogBound.lean#L37-L40","doc":"The corpus's p–n bond: a convex combination of the like-species bonds\n(`SymmetrySignAmGm.weight_of_convention` derives `w = 1/2 + δ_f/4`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}